/-!
# The abelian-conjugate-span argument in Section 12.6

The setup uses an actual isomorphism to the six-dimensional eight-point
permutation section. It defines V₁ from the marked element, V₅ as its
perpendicular, the source family H_z, the intrinsic two-core quotient,
and both spans by conjugation inside the original ambient group.

The current results establish the core-transfer steps of 12.6.24, all
four equivalences of 12.6.25 from the genuine F.9.1 hypotheses and the
centralizer equality, and the actual fusion inference in 12.6.27 from
abelianness at G_z. They also derive the nontrivial star image from the
contrary-nonabelian assumption, and prove the final order contradiction
on the literal quotient image.

The F.9.1 bridge and the odd-core, component and L₂(11) arguments of
12.6.26 remain to be proved. In particular this module does not assert
unconditional abelianness of V_H or completion of 12.6.24–27. The explicit
premises of the conditional consequences must be discharged in assembly.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
Section 12.6.2 and Lemma 12.6.27, printed pp.830–833, PDF pp.847–850.
-/
